      "content": "The pruning math is inverted: `resolved.slice(keep)` with a positive `keep` drops the oldest `keep` entries and keeps only `resolved.length - keep`, rather than keeping the newest `keep` resolved entries. Concrete failure: a run accumulates 50 resolved approval cards, then a 51st (open) request arrives → `keep = 50 - 1 = 49` → `resolved.slice(49)` keeps only 1 resolved entry → the list collapses from 51 to 2 entries, silently discarding 49 resolved approval-card history entries, and this repeats each time the cap is exceeded. Secondary case: when `open.length \u003e CAP`, `keep ≤ 0` and `Math.max(keep, 0) = 0` makes `slice(0)` retain all resolved entries, so the list stays over the cap. Fix by dropping exactly the overflow from the oldest resolved entries.",
      "suggestion_code": "              if (record.inputRequests.length \u003e INPUT_REQUESTS_CAP) {\n                const drop = Math.min(\n                  resolved.length,\n                  record.inputRequests.length - INPUT_REQUESTS_CAP\n                );\n                record.inputRequests = [...resolved.slice(drop), ...open];\n              }",
