      "thinking": "Confirmed. `resolved.slice(keep)` with positive `keep` returns entries from index `keep` onward — i.e., it keeps `resolved.length - keep` entries and drops the oldest `keep`. The intent (per the comment \"Prune oldest resolved entries when over cap\") is to keep the newest `keep` resolved entries.\n\nConcrete failure: 50 resolved requests + 1 new open → total 51 \u003e 50 → keep = 50 - 1 = 49 → `resolved.slice(49)` keeps only 1 resolved entry → list collapses to 2 entries, silently discarding 49 resolved approval-card history entries. This repeats every time the cap is exceeded.\n\nSecondary: when `open.length \u003e CAP`, keep ≤ 0 → `Math.max(keep, 0)` = 0 → `slice(0)` keeps ALL resolved, so the list exceeds the cap (all open retained by design is fine, but resolved should be dropped entirely).\n\nFix: drop exactly the overflow from the oldest resolved entries:\n\n```ts\nif (record.inputRequests.length \u003e INPUT_REQUESTS_CAP) {\n  const drop = Math.min(\n    resolved.length,\n    record.inputRequests.length - INPUT_REQUESTS_CAP\n  );\n  record.inputRequests = [...resolved.slice(drop), ...open];\n}\n```\n\nThis is a genuine correctness defect (silent data loss in the record's ring buffer, violating the documented cap semantics). Report it as bug/medium.\n\nEverything else I examined held up:\n- Dedupe/writeIf/seenKeys ordering is correct (mutations discarded when the write is skipped).\n- Atomic tmp+rename writes, per-session serialization chain never poisons.\n- Path traversal guarded by SESSION_ID_PATTERN + prefix check; tmp files excluded from recordIds.\n- Stage cap splice drops the oldest closed stage — correct.\n- Root/child attribution (rootOf/isRootScope/onlyIfExists filters) matches the documented eve event contracts (author verified against dist types and live runs).\n- Zombie detection semantics match the spec (approval-hang non-terminal only; error-loop by streak).\n- Sweep only deletes terminal records; corrupt-read failures are ca